    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's strange. When I look at the steel, it's the only thing that feels honest. Everything else was a lie—the glory, the oaths, the kingdom. But the edge of this blade... it's sharp, it's real, and it's the only thing that can actually provide some kind of release from this weight. Like it's the only way to finally reach the end of the chapter.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
